STEP 7  the self-play limit points W = (W_CC, W_CD, W_DC, W_DD):
        at the 16 VERTICES: 6 distinct points --
            (0, 0, 0, 1)   0000 0110 1000
            (0, 1/4, 1/4, 1/2)   0010 0100
            (1/4, 1/4, 1/4, 1/4)   0011 0101 1010 1100
            (1/2, 0, 0, 1/2)   0001 0111
            (1/2, 1/4, 1/4, 0)   1011 1101
            (1, 0, 0, 0)   1001 1110 1111
        on the CONTINUUM grid: 128001 distinct points
        every one has W_CD = W_DC exactly: True
        the 16-vertex set is contained in it: True
        denominators of the coordinates run from 1 to 316649 (20768 distinct); the vertex
        set uses only [1, 2, 4]
        STRUCTURE.  Strong lumping of {CC}|{CD,DC}|{DD} (both CD and DC send
        beta = (1-p~2)(1-p~3) to DD and gamma = p~2 p~3 to CC) gives the
        Markov-chain-tree weights, with a = p~1, d = p~4,
            X = d[(2-d)gamma + d beta],  Y = 2(1-a)d(1+a-d),
            Z = (1-a)[(1-a)gamma + (1+a)beta],   W = (X, Y/2, Y/2, Z)/(X+Y+Z),
        so the limit set is the union over the 81 strata (each p_i at 0 / interior / 1)
        of the images of finitely many RATIONAL maps of p; it is a 2-parameter family
        inside the plane W_CD = W_DC of the 3-simplex, not a finite list.  The six
        vertex points are the images of the corners; denominators are unbounded as the
        grid refines, which is exactly why the vertex census is finite and this is not.
        the eps^0 lumped formula reproduces the exact limit at 279222 of the 279222 points
        where it is non-degenerate (the rest need the eps-orders)

